- Yeah.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:14.040
Interestingly enough, it did,

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:16.270
you know, it carved out a
little personality, but anyway.

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:17.280
(Jacob and audience laughing)

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.410
This isn't your first
musical role though, right?

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.370
- No.
- Did you grow up

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.080
doing musical stuff?
- My first role ever

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.110
was a musical, and I
played the Cat in the Hat

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.558
in "Seussical the Musical."

00:07:26.558 --> 00:07:27.391
- Yes.
(audience exclaims)

00:07:27.391 --> 00:07:28.691
- Yeah, yeah.

00:07:28.691 --> 00:07:31.151
- Yes.
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:07:31.151 --> 00:07:32.850
Look at how proud you are.
(audience applauding)

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:33.728
- Yeah. Right now, like this.

00:07:33.728 --> 00:07:35.648
- Just so proud.
(audience applauding)

00:07:35.648 --> 00:07:37.813
I love it. I love it.

00:07:37.813 --> 00:07:39.990
I bet they knew Vin, you
know, from that photo.

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.288
They're like, "He's gonna make it."

00:07:41.288 --> 00:07:42.600
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:43.800
- Yeah. They might say that.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:45.405
- Just the confidence. I love-

00:07:45.405 --> 00:07:47.728
- I think they asked me to
leave the school after that.

00:07:47.728 --> 00:07:48.660
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:51.180
- No. Do you believe in mentorship?

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:53.040
'Cause I would've loved,
I came in as a teenager,

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.270
and I would've loved to have someone

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:55.740
to bounce stuff off of.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:57.420
Do you have any mentors in the industry?

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.400
- I mean, nothing so direct

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.470
'cause I kind of shy away from advice.

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:02.580
I'm kind of
- Yeah?

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:04.874
- I don't like being
told sort of what to do.

00:08:04.874 --> 00:08:06.090
But I think, just subconsciously,

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:07.680
the people that I've worked with-

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:08.882
- Are you a Scorpio?

00:08:08.882 --> 00:08:09.877
(Jacob titters)

00:08:09.877 --> 00:08:10.710
- Dunno what that means.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:12.180
- Okay. Oh, it's a-
- I'm a Cancer.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:13.195
- Oh, you're a Cancer. Okay.

00:08:13.195 --> 00:08:14.455
Okay.
- Little crab.

00:08:14.455 --> 00:08:15.288
- I like it.

00:08:15.288 --> 00:08:17.020
(Kelly laughs)

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:18.060
"I'm a little crab."

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.239
- Yes.
- No, I love that.

00:08:19.239 --> 00:08:20.072
Okay.

00:08:20.072 --> 00:08:21.720
I take advice only as advice.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.220
- Yeah, I just don't wanna get married

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:24.360
to any idea or anything.
- Yeah.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.403
I don't wanna get married. (laughs)

00:08:26.403 --> 00:08:27.761
(audience laughing)

00:08:27.761 --> 00:08:29.719
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:08:29.719 --> 00:08:30.552
There we go.

00:08:30.552 --> 00:08:32.681
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:08:32.681 --> 00:08:33.514
That's great.

00:08:33.514 --> 00:08:36.180
No, I do think that, 'cause
it's what makes you, you.

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:38.760
Your decision-making process. I get that.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:40.920
I hear that you're also
a Jack Kerouac fan.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:41.760
- I am.

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:44.070
- I feel like you're so young
for that, but that's cool.

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:45.420
- I feel like that's the only time

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.310
that you're supposed to
be a Jack Kerouac fan,

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:50.700
it's when you're young, and
then maybe when you're old you,

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:51.642
you can revisit.

00:08:51.642 --> 00:08:52.525
- Yeah.

00:08:52.525 --> 00:08:53.358
- But, yeah. Yeah.

00:08:53.358 --> 00:08:56.817
I kind of found, you know, on
the road at the right time,

00:08:56.817 --> 00:09:01.290
18, 19, you know, going
to America, leaving home.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:03.150
You know, I've got fire on my feet

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:06.900
and, you know, I'm trying to
find the feeling in things.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:11.490
So it was like a companion,
you know, novel to my,

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:13.800
sort of coming to America
and everything like that.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:14.667
- Yeah. That was "Jane Eyre" for me

00:09:14.667 --> 00:09:16.320
- Oh, yeah?
- That book changed me.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:17.190
Yeah. That was just that.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:19.050
I love that book.

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:21.480
'Cause I moved out to LA
before "Idol" or whatever,

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:23.310
and, yeah, I got very lonely.

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:25.200
Like, I can get lonely really quickly.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:26.640
It's nice to have things like that.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:28.830
- Yeah.
- Like give you solace.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:31.080
- There's section in Kerouac's book,

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:32.100
'cause he's going and going

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:34.920
and traveling across America,
searching for his pal,

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:37.320
and sort of towards the end,

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:39.450
he's so sort of tired and weary.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:40.530
And there's this one sentence

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:42.030
and it's highlighted in my copy of it.

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:44.220
And he said, "I wish I could see someone

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:46.350
that had known me for
more than five minutes."

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.250
And that's paraphrasing
it or something like that.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.083
- Yeah.

00:09:49.083 --> 00:09:50.040
- But that was the line
- Really deeply knew.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.830
- that really kind of rocked
me from that book, you know?

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:56.010
This idea of having someone
that knows your soul

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:57.937
and movements, not just kind of

00:09:57.937 --> 00:09:59.220
- Yeah.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:01.260
- who you are or what you've
done or, you know, that kind-

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.570
- I had to train myself
to be good at small talk.

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:05.640
I was not, that was not my thing.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:07.350
- Yeah. I'm not there yet.
- I'm amazing at it now,

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:09.270
but I had to train myself.

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:12.210
'Cause I'm deeply, I like
wanna know everything

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:14.130
and I wanna get in a real
conversation and know someone.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:15.343
And that really hard for me to do.

00:10:15.343 --> 00:10:17.340
- I just sort of will walk away.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.810
- Yeah. (chuckles)
- I'm in that phase.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:20.555
- That's a nice approach as well.

00:10:20.555 --> 00:10:23.198
- If you act strange
enough, people would like...

00:10:23.198 --> 00:10:24.031
(Kelly laughs)

00:10:24.031 --> 00:10:24.864
- He's odd.

00:10:24.864 --> 00:10:25.697
You're like, "Yeah, I'll get away

00:10:25.697 --> 00:10:26.609
if I'm odd."
- Yeah, you get away

00:10:26.609 --> 00:10:27.442
if you're odd, you know?

00:10:27.442 --> 00:10:28.275
- I love that.

00:10:28.275 --> 00:10:29.617
Well, let's do another break everybody.

00:10:29.617 --> 00:10:32.567
"Priscilla" is in theaters
nationwide starting this Friday.

